      "message": "fix(motion): read a return run beside a tab against the tab core\n\nThe second review of #2705 found that tab_clear::departed drops a return\nrun that goes along the tab at a constant distance (a tab end at or past\nthe near floor corner of a notch narrower than 2 D). New module tab_kerf:\nthe two cuts beside a tab are read against the tab line without the parts\nthat the end kerfs take. Only the part of a cut that is in the disc of\nradius D about the tab end, and runs away from it, is skipped. A cut under\nD from the core holds the loop with a tabs: note.\n\nRefs #2561\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
